tained clusters when processing. That is safe.\n\nThus:\n\n- Build full tree with all clusters.\n- Compute stability for all clusters (using formula). Only retain those with size >= min_cluster_size.\n- Sort the retained clusters as described.\n- Selection as above, using ancestor/descendant relationships in the full tree (including dropped clusters as nodes, but they are not in selection list).\n\nImplementation steps in Python:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate case structure\n    min_size = case['min_cluster_size']\n    clusters = case['clusters']\n    parent_map = case['parent']\n\n    # build dicts\n    cluster_dict = {c['cluster_id']: c for c in clusters}\n    # validate all cluster_ids present\n    # precompute children adjacency\n    children = {cid: [] for cid in cluster_dict}\n    for cid in cluster_dict:\n        p = parent_map.get(cid)\n        if p is not None:\n            children[p].append(cid)\n    # also roots: clusters with None parent\n\n    # compute stabilities for all (or only retained? we compute for all but only keep retained)\n    stabilities = {}\n    for cid, c in cluster_dict.items():\n        birth = c['birth_lambda']\n        exits = c['point_exit_lambdas']\n        stab = sum(max(0, l - birth) for l in exits)\n        stabilities[cid] = stab\n\n    # filter retained: size >= min_size\n    retained_ids = [cid for cid, c in cluster_dict.items() if c['size'] >= min_size]\n    # Note: we need to ensure that if a cluster is not retained, it's still in the tree for descendant/ancestor checks,\n    # but we won't consider it for selection.\n\n    # Prepare list of (cid, stability) for retained clusters\n    retained_list = [(cid, stabilities[cid]) for cid in retained_ids]\n    # sort by -stability, cid\n    retained_list.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\n\n    # Precompute ancestors for each cluster (list of ancestor IDs, upward excluding self)\n    ancestors = {}\n    for cid in cluster_dict:\n        anc = []\n        cur = parent_map.g